WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.407 --> 00:00:00.990
JANET KUO: Hi.

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:03.720
I'm Janet Kuo, software
engineer at Google

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.240
and also co-chair of KubeCon.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.460
Today, I did a keynote on
Kubernetes project update,

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.230
and I'd like to give
you a recap on it.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.840
So I had a Kubernetes look back,
and a history of Kubernetes,

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:22.800
starting from Google created
Borg, and then the Linux

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.100
containers, and then
the Docker containers,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.320
and then Omega projects.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:32.130
And then we open sourced
Kubernetes, and until this day,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.590
Kubernetes has
become very popular,

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:38.250
and we have over
31,000 contributors.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.880
And it's also one of the highest
velocity projects on GitHub.

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.170
Today, Kubernetes is
very stable and mature,

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.990
and we are celebrating
the five-years anniversary

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.580
for Kubernetes.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.330
And the next focus
in the community

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:57.300
will be on extensibility.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:01.130
I expect more people to
extend on top of Kubernets.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.140
And then scalability--
I expect we

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.410
keep improving the scalability
limits on Kubernetes.

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.610
And the third focus will
be around reliability.

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:16.750
We need to fix the cascading
failures more holistically,

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.220
and we need to do it
together, as a community.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.950
I expect you to
contribute to Kubernetes.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.860
And if you have questions,
feel free to meet us

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:27.480
at Google's booth.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.240
Thank you.

